.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH parameterize 1  "parameterize " 
.SH NAME
parameterize \- Turn repeated literals into variables
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBparameterize\fR [\fB\-\-literal\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Turn repeated literals into variables
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-literal\fR \fI<TEXT>\fR
A literal to parameterize (repeat with \-\-as; pairs apply directly)
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Variable name for the preceding \-\-literal
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Snippet name
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  fg parameterize deploy \-\-literal eu\-west\-1 \-\-as region
